# TARGET ARCHITECTURE: aarch64 (ARM64) | v0.16.4 | on-prem/rocky9
# ARM64-specific syscall mapping; reconcile against this product/version ARM64 STIG or approved baseline.
# Enterprise Linux Audit v0.16.4  |  [on-prem/rocky9]
# Tier: tier-2-core-security
# Purpose: systemd persistence and optional cron/loader persistence
# Source/authority: Enterprise SOC/IR minimum
# Architecture: aarch64 (b64 only). No x86/compat b32 syscall rules.
# Release state: engineering candidate; NOT independently certified STIG compliant.


-a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/systemd/system -F perm=wa -k t2_persistence
# OPTIONAL existing locations:
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/cron.d -F perm=wa -k t2_persistence
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/var/spool/cron -F perm=wa -k t2_persistence
# -a always,exit -F arch=b64 -F dir=/etc/ld.so.conf.d -F perm=wa -k t2_ldconfig
